# acro_flight.expect — assert ARM → TAKEOFF → FLYING AND the in-flight switch to
# ACRO (rate) mode, driven by the `acro` scenario token (CTRL_FLAG_MODE). ACRO
# rate tracking itself is checked numerically from trajectory.csv.
# ARM→TAKEOFF→FLYING に加え、acro トークン(CTRL_FLAG_MODE)による飛行中の ACRO（角速度）
# モード切替を検証する。ACRO レート追従は trajectory.csv で数値確認する。
exit 0
log_contains any "ARM accepted"                       # IDLE_GROUND → ARMED_GROUND
log_contains any "Takeoff detected"                   # ARMED_GROUND → TAKEOFF
log_contains any "Takeoff complete"                   # TAKEOFF → FLYING
log_contains any "Mode change: STABILIZE"             # STABILIZE → ACRO (requestModeChange accepted)
log_contains any "DISARM accepted"                    # FLYING → IDLE_GROUND (pilot DISARM)
# Spec 2026-06-11: mode changes are accepted on the GROUND too (IDLE/ARMED_GROUND).
# The acro switch is already on when the throttle-up row starts, so the mode now
# changes in ARMED_GROUND — BEFORE takeoff (it used to be deferred to FLYING).
# 仕様 2026-06-11: モード変更は地上（IDLE/ARMED_GROUND）でも受理される。acro スイッチは
# スロットル上げの行で既に ON のため、モード変更は ARMED_GROUND で — 離陸「前」に起こる
# （以前は FLYING まで保留されていた）。
order "ARM accepted" "Mode change: STABILIZE"         # ground mode change after ARM
order "Mode change: STABILIZE" "Takeoff complete"     # ...and before the takeoff completes
order "Mode change: STABILIZE" "DISARM accepted"      # flies in ACRO before disarm
# Numerical gates over the rate-doublet flight window (G2/G3). 飛行窓 [7.0,9.7]s。
metric att_rmse < 3.0  in 7.0 9.7    # G2: ESKF roll/pitch tracks truth through the doublets
metric tilt_max < 25.0 in 7.0 9.7    # G3: attitude bounded — no tumble during ACRO
# G4 (duty): ACRO rate doublets briefly saturate the motors BY DESIGN (broadband
# excitation, roadmap §3.1.3), so motor duty is intentionally NOT gated for ACRO.
# G4(duty): ACRO のレートダブレットは設計上モータを瞬間飽和させるため未ゲート。
